No. NETHACKOPTIONS is an environment variable, not a config file option.
You probably don't need to futz with that; assuming you're on Windows,
just create a text file called defaults.nh in the same directory that
contains the nethack.exe (or nethackw.exe) that should contain config
options.  See http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Options

